<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies seen frost free for the week - EC.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies seen frost free for the week - EC.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairie grainbelt was forecast to be free of frost through the week due to a westerly flow of air and high moisture content in the air, an Environment Canada meteorologist said.</p>
<p>&quot;No, there's no risk at all of frost for tomorrow. There's too much moisture in the air to get close to freezing and for the week there doesn't seem to be any threat of frost because this westerly flow should keep the Arctic airmass off the Prairies,&quot; meteorologist Clarence Spelchak said.</p>
<p>Western Manitoba saw lows of +4.0 Celsius Sunday while Regina, Saskatchewan, saw a low of +2.0 Celsius, he said.</p>
<p>((Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
